  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4425:The intention behind an access arrangement is to meet the particular needs of an 
individual
> specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4426:student with a disability, without affecting the integrity of the assessment. 
Access
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4427:arrangements are the principal way in which awarding bodies comply with the duty 
under the
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4428:Equality Act 2010 to make ‘reasonable adjustments’.
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4429:
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4430:Access arrangements should always be processed at the start of the course. 
Students will
> specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4431:then know what is available and have the access arrangement(s) in place for 
assessment.
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4432:
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4433:Reasonable adjustments
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4434:
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4435:The Equality Act 2010 requires an awarding organisation to make reasonable 
adjustments
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4436:where a person with a disability would be at a substantial disadvantage in 
undertaking an
> specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4437:assessment. The awarding organisation is required to take reasonable steps to 
overcome
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4438:that disadvantage.
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4439:
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4440:A reasonable adjustment for a particular person may be unique to that individual 
and
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4441:therefore might not be in the list of available access arrangements.
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4451:
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4452:●  the likely impact of the adjustment on the student with the disability and 
other students.
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4453:
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4454:An adjustment will not be approved if it involves unreasonable costs to the 
awarding
> specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4455:organisation, timeframes or affects the security or integrity of the assessment. 
This is
  specs\edexcel\history-1HI0.md:4456:because the adjustment is not ‘reasonable’.
