+    "lesson": 6,
+    "field": "exam_tip_html",
+    "find": "<p data-narration-id=\"n17\">For “Explain One Cause” questions (4 marks), make sure you identify the cause clearly in your first sentence, then develop it with three further linked points. Use connectives like “this was because,” “which meant that,” and “as a result” to show a chain of reasoning. For example: “One cause of détente was the cost of the arms race. This was because both superpowers were spending huge sums on nuclear weapons, which diverted resources from their economies. As a result, both sides had a financial incentive to agree limits on nuclear weapons, leading to SALT 1 in 1972.”</p>",
