+    "find": "<p data-narration-id=\"n20\">For “How Far Do You Agree” questions (16 marks) on the end of the Cold War, examiners want you to analyse <em>multiple factors</em> and reach a <em>judgement</em>. Don’t just list factors — compare them. For example: “While Gorbachev’s reforms were important, they would not have succeeded without Reagan’s economic pressure, which forced the USSR to the negotiating table. However, the fundamental weakness of the Soviet economy was arguably the root cause, as it made reform necessary in the first place.” A clear, reasoned conclusion will push you into the top level.</p>",
